def cmd_journal_query(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:
    """T-12144 (SPEC-0190 rule 10) — the ONE request-scoped ReadScope for the `journal query` seam.

    THE SHAPE IT REMOVES, MEASURED ON THIS REPO 2026-09-05 (`journal query --dispatch-status`, 96
    segments / 16 live worktree journals): the wave view calls `_dispatch_status_events` TWICE — once
    directly to seed the task set from the dispatch-boundary rows, then again through
    `_dispatch_events_tail_first_multi` to classify them — so ONE request folded the 16-journal union
    32 times and handed 1,057,569 rows to the parser over a ~530,000-row corpus. Two views, each
    owning its own fold, which is exactly the composition rule 10 governs.

    IT REUSES THE EXISTING PRIMITIVE, IT DOES NOT ADD ONE (CHARTER §P1 filter 1). `_dispatch_events_memo()`
    is the T-11438 request-scoped memo already installed at `_debt_echo_lines` and
    `_unmonitored_dispatch_view`; this is a third WIRING SITE for it, not a second reader and not a
    per-view cache — every call still resolves through the same injected `_dispatch_status_events`
    union, and nothing survives the scope.

    THIS SCOPE IS HALF THE FIX; THE OTHER HALF IS NOT A SCOPE AT ALL. The dispatch memo alone leaves
    the request at 1.079x, and that residual is a SINGLE identifiable double-read: this checkout's own
    journal is opened twice — once as the local leg, once again as a member of the live-worktree union
    it is itself a member of (33,917 of 462,419 lines). It is removed at its source instead, by the
    leg-list de-duplication in `journal.py#_dispatch_status_events`, which drops only reads whose every
    row the identity dedup already discarded. Together the two take the seam to rows_parse_ratio
    1.000 and wall 22.56s -> 11.87s, so NO `reads.exemptions[]` entry is owed and none is declared.

    `rows_memo` IS DELIBERATELY NOT INSTALLED HERE, and the omission is measured rather than reasoned.
    It would PESSIMISE this seam: `rows_memo` DECLARES the logical journal, which converts the dispatch
    union's bounded TAIL read of the live segment into a full 96-segment fold (14 folds -> 108, 12.6s
    -> 22.3s, measured 2026-09-05). A ReadScope is only free where the reader was going to read the
    whole declared journal anyway. The plain `journal query --type/--grep/--since` path folds this
    repo's journal exactly ONCE already, so there is nothing there for a scope to remove either.

    IT IS NOT A CACHE (rule 10's named retirement). The manager is request-scoped and nothing survives
    the `with` — including after an exception; it memoises its OWN reader's result, never a second
    reader, so no answer this verb gives can move, only the number of times the same bytes are read."""
    global _JOURNAL_QUERY_TASK_HORIZON, _JOURNAL_QUERY_CARDS
    prior = (_JOURNAL_QUERY_TASK_HORIZON, _JOURNAL_QUERY_CARDS)
    _JOURNAL_QUERY_CARDS = {}                                     # T-13311 — this invocation's only
    _JOURNAL_QUERY_TASK_HORIZON = _journal_query_task_horizon()
    try:
        with journal_mod.reads_span("journal query"), _dispatch_events_memo():   # T-12840 — see graph query's
            return _cmd_journal_query_scoped(args)
    finally:
        _JOURNAL_QUERY_TASK_HORIZON, _JOURNAL_QUERY_CARDS = prior


# T-13311 (SPEC-0190 rule 4) — the TASK horizon reader of ONE `journal query` invocation and its card
# memo, installed only for its `with` (saved/restored like `_DISPATCH_EVENTS_MEMO`) and None everywhere
# else, so every other caller of the dispatch readers keeps its shape. Nothing survives the invocation.
_JOURNAL_QUERY_TASK_HORIZON = None
_JOURNAL_QUERY_CARDS = None


def _journal_query_task_horizon():
    """T-13311 — tid -> the card's task horizon (`audit.audit_task_horizon`: created_at - 2 d) or None
    (no card / no created_at / unreadable => no proven floor). The card is the MAIN checkout's — the
    one the strand reader reads — through `_main_task_card`, so each card is parsed ONCE per invocation."""
    def _horizon(tid):
        try:
            card = _main_task_card(tid)
        except Exception:
            return None
        return audit.audit_task_horizon(card) if isinstance(card, dict) else None
    return _horizon


