# Plan FSM (D-0034, amended T-0114; EXTENDED T-0316 per the accepted governing plan
# plan-lifecycle-delivery-parity-redesign; `trial` INSERTED T-0336 per SPEC-0035 + the sibling
# amendment add-a-controlled-real-data-trial-stage-between-pla). The authoritative stage sequence
# mirrors `task stage` but on ONE `status` field (no status/stage duality — plans have no picker,
# §Stage model Decision 1):
#   draft → specs → trial → accepted → decomposition → executing → postcheck → realized   (+ terminals partial|rejected|cancelled)
# `decomposition` (SPEC-0070) is the gated CUT stage between `accepted` and `executing`: the plan is
# sliced into task cards here, and a mandatory external decomposition-fidelity audit of the card SET
# gates entry to `executing`. Inserting it auto-makes `plan-stage-entry:decomposition` a VALID binding
# suffix (`_is_valid_plan_stage_entry`), same as the `trial` insertion above (T-0337).
# `trial` (SPEC-0035) is a controlled real-data design-convergence stage between `specs` and `accepted`.
# Its entry is OWNER-INVOKED and only for trial-ELIGIBLE plans (SPEC-0035 rule 2); non-eligible plans
# take the SKIP path `specs → accepted` directly. The `accepted` entry-gate is therefore TWO-BRANCH
# (`trial → accepted` converged OR `specs → accepted` skip — SPEC-0035 rules 1-2), handled as a special
# case in cmd_plan_stage's FSM-edge validation. Additive: pre-existing draft/accepted/realized plans
# stay valid (the SKIP branch IS the unchanged current path). The SPEC-0034 BODY edits + SPEC-0035's
# plan-stage-entry:trial binding are a SEPARATE change-set (T-0337); the `plan-stage-entry:trial`
# token becomes a VALID binding suffix here automatically (it is now in PLAN_STAGE_SEQUENCE).
PLAN_STAGE_SEQUENCE = ("draft", "specs", "trial", "accepted", "decomposition", "executing", "postcheck", "realized")
# Terminals: `realized` is the DONE terminal (the sequence tail); partial/rejected/cancelled are the
# wont-do/abandoned terminals reachable from any active (non-terminal) stage.

# Active = every non-terminal stage (the `plan list` default view + the close/reject/to-idea guards).

PLAN_STATUSES = tuple(dict.fromkeys(PLAN_STAGE_SEQUENCE + vocab.PLAN_TERMINAL))  # ordered, de-duped union
PLAN_RESOLUTIONS = ("realized", "partial")
# Linear plan stages STRICTLY BEFORE `executing` (= draft,specs,trial,accepted,decomposition) — the
# SPEC-0070 §5 claim-block window: a task whose cited plan is at one of these is NOT claimable (the cut
# must pass the decomposition→executing fidelity gate before any card is built). Derived from the
# sequence (ONE source) so inserting/removing a stage cannot desync the set.
PLAN_PRE_EXECUTING_STAGES = frozenset(PLAN_STAGE_SEQUENCE[:PLAN_STAGE_SEQUENCE.index("executing")])
